    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Operator Precedence"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Order of Operation"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Operator precedence describes the order in which operations are performed in\nan arithmetic expression."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Multiplication (*) and division (/) have higher precedence than\naddition (+) and subtraction (-)."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 100 + 50 * 3;",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = (100 + 50) * 3;",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 100 / 50 * 3;",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
